---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';
const C = SITE.checker;
---
<Base title="Install OKtoPress on Your Print Shop Website" description="Add OKtoPress to your print shop website with one line of code or the WordPress plugin shortcode [oktopress].">
<div class="wrap narrow">
  <h1>Install OKtoPress on your shop's website</h1>
  <p class="muted">Customers check their art, see a price range and send you the lead. Uploads go to the OKtoPress service inside the embed and never touch your website's server. New here? See <a href="/how-it-works">how it works</a> and <a href="/features">features</a>.</p>
  <section id="embed"><h2>1. Create your free shop account</h2>
    <p>Sign up with your email, shop name and website. Your dashboard gives you a ready-made snippet with your own Shop ID. It only loads on the websites you register.</p>
    <p><a class="btn" href={SITE.signup}>Start free</a></p>
    <p class="muted">Already signed up? <a href={SITE.login}>Log in to your dashboard</a>.</p>
    <h2>2. Set your prices</h2>
    <p>Start from the starter price grid and adjust it to how you price jobs.</p>
    <h2>3. Paste one line of code</h2>
    <p>Paste the snippet from your dashboard into your site. On WordPress, install the OKtoPress plugin and use the shortcode <code>[oktopress]</code> or the block. Wix support is planned. Style it to match your site's colours, font and corners from your dashboard.</p>
  </section>
</div>
</Base>
